  "verdict": "CLASS G IS NON-VACUOUS AND DISCRIMINATING. An explicit stochastic system satisfies ALL TEN \u00a78.3 conditions simultaneously (barrier lowered 0.250 -> 0.107 with mean first-passage 386 -> 187; agency variance 0.50; identity diffusion 0.020 against a measured critical 0.100; lambda_perp -1.01, lambda_par +0.000; correlation power 0.22; aperiodic (sup-norm exact-period error 0.041 >> 1e-06); incommensurable drive; gate factorization exact (rank-1 residual 1.7e-16) with a gate that genuinely closes; and the external field is NOT in the endogenous span (projection residual 0.60 against a deliberately generous basis). So the ten conditions are MUTUALLY CONSISTENT: Class G is not empty by over-specification, and \u00a7\u00a78-10 stand as written, now with a satisfiability witness. The criterion also DISCRIMINATES: every near-miss in \u00a78.3's own filter table fails, and each fails a condition the table predicts -- damping fails ['2_agency_positive', '5_tangential_protected', '6_long_correlation', '7_aperiodic'], ungated forcing fails ['3_identity_subcritical', '9_gate_factorization'], endogenous feedback fails ['1_barrier_lowered', '10_not_endogenous'], coercion fails ['2_agency_positive', '9_gate_factorization'], a commensurable drive fails ['7_aperiodic', '8_incommensurable']. The conjunction therefore has real exclusionary content rather than being satisfied by everything. SCOPE: this establishes logical consistency and discrimination ONLY. It says nothing about whether any biological, psychological or theological process instantiates Class G -- precisely the question \u00a78.3 declines to answer -- and domain-emptiness in any particular substrate remains possible and untested here.",
  "figures": [
